[[:db/retract 17592186125189 :question/answer-fields 17592186123704] {:db/id 17592186125189 :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=1.$ Given that the point $P(1,-1,2)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}={x}^{2}(2xy-1)$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(1,-1).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,-1) & =(1)^{2}(2(1)(-1)-1)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(1,-1) & ={f}_{y}(1,-1)(y+1) \\\\ z-2 & =-3(y+1) \\\\ z-2 & =-3y-3 \\\\ z & =-3y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,-1,2)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ z=-3y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=-3y-1$ (or $-3y-z-1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,-3,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,-3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =j-3\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $j-3\\,k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a315569d-b4ce-597c-a11e-e51ae4013a54"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a315569d-b4ce-597c-a11e-e51ae4013a54" :answer-field/id #uuid "a315569d-b4ce-597c-a11e-e51ae4013a54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-25cf98fa-a5b3-5e6b-b710-84fa1db64ec9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fd44ef3e-d356-53fe-b14e-c4931ae0f4a0" "answer-5de2add0-6423-5754-a07f-96730ef51cc3" "answer-db135884-f54c-58f1-b6d6-52b5e9137f78" "answer-bccf173f-8570-55d3-b189-673a90a1c377" "answer-25cf98fa-a5b3-5e6b-b710-84fa1db64ec9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd44ef3e-d356-53fe-b14e-c4931ae0f4a0" :answer/id #uuid "fd44ef3e-d356-53fe-b14e-c4931ae0f4a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2j+\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5de2add0-6423-5754-a07f-96730ef51cc3" :answer/id #uuid "5de2add0-6423-5754-a07f-96730ef51cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j-2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db135884-f54c-58f1-b6d6-52b5e9137f78" :answer/id #uuid "db135884-f54c-58f1-b6d6-52b5e9137f78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2j+3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bccf173f-8570-55d3-b189-673a90a1c377" :answer/id #uuid "bccf173f-8570-55d3-b189-673a90a1c377" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25cf98fa-a5b3-5e6b-b710-84fa1db64ec9" :answer/id #uuid "25cf98fa-a5b3-5e6b-b710-84fa1db64ec9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "j-3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124444 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-05b78370-0b37-5800-aa28-6b6b17964b90"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-05b78370-0b37-5800-aa28-6b6b17964b90" :question/id #uuid "05b78370-0b37-5800-aa28-6b6b17964b90" :question/math-academy-id "q-71216" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=1.$ Given that the point $P(1,0,-1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=x{e}^{xy}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(1,0,-1)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(1,0)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,0) & =1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 0}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1,0)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(1,0)}(y-0) \\\\ z-(-1) & =(-1)y \\\\ z & =-y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,0,-1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ z=-y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e94262ee-f4dd-5ac5-a015-9c5cf4798aa0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e94262ee-f4dd-5ac5-a015-9c5cf4798aa0" :answer-field/id #uuid "e94262ee-f4dd-5ac5-a015-9c5cf4798aa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d4018ef0-2dba-5e3f-8527-3ea960bf4de4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8d3f6706-e60e-5d15-b360-58385706ee4f" "answer-40205211-9c82-5bbc-b29c-5211d1a45bbb" "answer-3f49be2f-9fbd-57d9-8743-c7f792e14929" "answer-d4018ef0-2dba-5e3f-8527-3ea960bf4de4" "answer-645649e7-f6ca-5dcf-a129-028646be2cfe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d3f6706-e60e-5d15-b360-58385706ee4f" :answer/id #uuid "8d3f6706-e60e-5d15-b360-58385706ee4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ z=-2y+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40205211-9c82-5bbc-b29c-5211d1a45bbb" :answer/id #uuid "40205211-9c82-5bbc-b29c-5211d1a45bbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ z=-2y-1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f49be2f-9fbd-57d9-8